// markdownlint-cli2 runner options. Rules live in `.markdownlint.jsonc`, which
// this tool also reads; this file only says WHICH FILES to lint.
{
  // Derive the exclusions from `.gitignore` instead of restating them.
  //
  // Every tree worth skipping here is already gitignored: `node_modules/`,
  // `/output/**` (run evidence and adapter output), `/evidence/**` (permanent
  // snapshots), `backend/modules/output/**`, and `frontend/dist/`. Several
  // contain BACKUPS OF OTHER REPOSITORIES' markdown that the portfolio tooling
  // captured — linting those reports style opinions about files nobody edits
  // here, and it dominated the result: a bare run walks 541 files and reports
  // 8,679 findings, of which ~8,400 are in trees this repo does not author.
  //
  // A hand-written copy of that list would be a second source of truth that
  // drifts the first time a generated directory is added. `.gitignore` already
  // answers "is this ours?", so this defers to it.
  //
  // Verified 2026-08-11: identical result to passing the five exclusions as
  // explicit globs — 56 files, 294 findings.
  //
  // No `.markdownlintignore` ships alongside this. One was written and removed:
  // the editor extension lints OPEN DOCUMENTS, not the tree, so it never had
  // the node_modules problem this solves — and the ignore file's own `#`
  // comments parse as ATX headings, so it generated about thirty Problems-panel
  // warnings about itself. It fixed nothing the panel showed and added noise.
  "gitignore": true
}
